            <ArticleTitle>Early-warning signals for critical transitions.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>53-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1038/nature08227</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Complex dynamical systems, ranging from ecosystems to financial markets and the climate, can have tipping points at which a sudden shift to a contrasting dynamical regime may occur. Although predicting such critical points before they are reached is extremely difficult, work in different scientific fields is now suggesting the existence of generic early-warning signals that may indicate for a wide class of systems if a critical threshold is approaching.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
